::MCR_U02_L07_Quiz_Q01::
Question ID: MCR_U02_L07_Quiz_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.AR.7
Question:
A theater row has 12 seats. A group has 50 people. What is the least viable number of rows needed?
{
=A. 5 rows#Correct. 50 divided by 12 is about 4.17, so 5 whole rows are needed.
~B. 4.17 rows#This is the decimal result, but rows must be whole.
~C. 6 rows#Six rows works but is not the least viable number.
~D. 3 rows#Three rows hold only 36 people, which is not enough.
}
